@@ -0,0 +1,188 @@
+# Replay a signed FieldLog halt on Android
+
+Use public Mixer commit `ad295143090e4c975564895030d81e5620b20253` and the
+accompanying test-only patch. Use the supplied `packet` and stock `mixer`
+together. The APK uses one Android development runtime for FieldLog on `beta`.
+The fixture publishes baseline sequence 1, then reviewed sequence 2 at 90%.
+It admits a signed halt at sequence 3 for the reviewed artifact at zero rollout.
+
+## Start the configured origin
+
+Use arm64 macOS with the locked test dependencies, Elixir 1.20.4 on OTP 29,
+PostgreSQL 17, OpenSSL, and Python. Reserve loopback ports 5432 and 47301.
+Use a new private run directory and absolute paths throughout.
+
+```sh
+git apply --check "$handoff/android-halt-v64.patch"
+git apply "$handoff/android-halt-v64.patch"
+export packet="$handoff/packet"
+(cd "$handoff" && shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS)
+(cd "$packet" && shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS)
+export mixer="$handoff/mixer"
+driver="$PWD/tests/integration/fieldlog-android-halt/evidence.py"
+run=$(mktemp -d "$PWD/verification/local/android-halt-run.XXXXXXXX")
+(
+  cd hosted
+  MIX_ENV=test HEX_OFFLINE=1 mix deps.get --check-locked
+  ./scripts/replay-configured-release.sh --fieldlog-halt \
+    "$packet/delivery-android" "$mixer" "$run"
+)
+```
+
+Run the last subshell in its own terminal. Wait for `$run/ready.json`. The
+fixture allows 10 minutes for the sample and 10 more after commit for final
+readback. If you need a new run, stop the owned fixture and confirm cleanup
+before starting with a new run directory.
+
+Start the relay in a second terminal. The relay prints its assigned port.
+It forwards the exact Android update scope and reviewed artifact from Phoenix.
+
+```sh
+python3 -B "$driver" relay "$packet" "$run"
+```
+
+To run the short host control, pass `--fieldlog-halt-control` with a different
+empty run directory. That control provides synthetic installation IDs and
+counts and completes without the relay.
+
+## Capture the installed comparison
+
+Use one owned API 36 arm64 emulator, its private ADB server port, and its exact
+serial. Use two fresh Android users on that emulator so both app data directories
+survive the comparison. You can also use two owned AVDs sequentially if the
+image lacks secondary users. Keep the active AVD's data through the offline
+check. Keep unrelated devices and ADB servers outside this run.
+
+```sh
+pkg=dev.fieldlog.generatedr90.calculation
+activity="$pkg/dev.fieldlog.generatedr90.androidhost.PublicActivity"
+apk="$packet/FieldLog-calculation-debug-api36.apk"
+apk_port=$(cat "$packet/delivery-android/Installed/port.txt")
+d() { adb -P "$adb_port" -s "$serial" "$@"; }
+state() { d exec-out run-as "$pkg" --user "$1" cat files/signed-checklist/recovery/state.json; }
+workspace() { d exec-out run-as "$pkg" --user "$1" cat files/FieldLog/workspace.json; }
+spool() { d exec-out run-as "$pkg" --user "$1" cat files/signed-checklist/artifact.partial; }
+screen_xml() {
+  d shell uiautomator dump "$device_xml" >/dev/null &&
+    d exec-out cat "$device_xml"
+}
+d shell getprop ro.build.version.sdk
+d shell getprop ro.product.cpu.abi
+d install --user "$active_user" "$apk"
+d reverse "tcp:$apk_port" "tcp:$relay_port"
+d shell am start --user "$active_user" -n "$activity"
+```
+
+Set `device_xml` to a new path in `/data/local/tmp` on the owned emulator.
+Record the current Android user, API, ABI, and serial. Pull the installed APK
+from the path returned by `d shell pm path --user "$active_user" "$pkg"`.
+Compare the pulled APK SHA-256 to `packet/build-receipt.json`. Verify the
+installed package source for the pending user too.
+
+1. In the active user, tap **Open signed checklist**. Wait for
+   **Signed checklist | Sequence 2** and the percentages 33%, 100%, and 0%.
+   Compare the FieldLog workspace with the packet seed. Save the live
+   readback, tap **Done**, and save the retired readback.
+
+   ```sh
+   screen_xml > "$run/active-before.xml"
+   state "$active_user" > "$run/active-live.json"
+   workspace "$active_user" > "$run/active-before.workspace"
+   d shell pidof -s "$pkg" > "$run/active-before.pid"
+   # Tap Done and wait for the dialog to close.
+   state "$active_user" > "$run/active-retired.json"
+   ```
+
+2. Create or select the exact owned pending Android user. For a second user on
+   the same AVD, run `d shell cmd package install-existing --user "$pending_user" "$pkg"`
+   and switch with `d shell am switch-user "$pending_user"`. Wait for that
+   user's unlocked launcher before starting the activity. Arm the relay before
+   the pending user's first checklist fetch.
+
+   ```sh
+   printf 'truncate-once\n' > "$run/fault-next.new"
+   mv "$run/fault-next.new" "$run/fault-next"
+   d shell am start --user "$pending_user" -n "$activity"
+   # Tap Open signed checklist and wait for the terminal error label.
+   screen_xml > "$run/pending-before.xml"
+   state "$pending_user" > "$run/pending-before.json"
+   spool "$pending_user" > "$run/pending-before.partial"
+   workspace "$pending_user" > "$run/pending-before.workspace"
+   python3 -B "$driver" sample "$packet" "$run"
+   ```
+
+   The relay closes the connection after 1,024 bytes and keeps the original
+   content length. The pending installation must show **The signed calculation
+   could not be opened** and retain the exact wire prefix in its spool. Its
+   recovery state must have accepted sequence 0 and no candidate. The adverse
+   count describes this deliberately induced transport failure. It does not
+   measure guest crashes or population health.
+
+   If an installation receives a 204 before commit and never gets an offer,
+   its generated ID may be outside the 90% cohort. Re-enroll only that
+   disposable profile from fresh app data and repeat its pre-halt step. Bound
+   the pre-halt enrollment to three attempts per role. Keep every profile
+   that already supplied accepted evidence. If the fault marker was consumed
+   but the pending proof does not match, stop that run and retain its result.
+
+3. Wait for `$run/committed.json`. It contains the stock CLI result, the exact
+   retry result comparison, and the single scoped audit event. Both device
+   users must now check the same installed origin again. In the pending user
+   tap **Check for update**, let the error settle, and capture the same files
+   as `pending-after.json`, `pending-after.partial`, `pending-after.xml`, and
+   `pending-after.workspace`. Tap **Done** and force-stop the exact pending
+   user app before switching back. In the active user, open the checklist or
+   tap **Check for update** and confirm sequence 2 remains usable. Tap **Done**
+   and wait for retirement. The relay must record an empty 204 for each ID
+   after commit.
+
+4. Remove the reverse mapping and stop the owned relay. Put the emulator in
+   airplane mode and check that both default routes are absent. Force-stop
+   the active app, confirm that its process is gone, and start it again in
+   the active user.
+
+   ```sh
+   d reverse --remove "tcp:$apk_port"
+   # Interrupt the owned relay and wait for exit.
+   d reverse --list > "$run/offline.reverse"
+   d shell cmd connectivity airplane-mode enable
+   d shell svc wifi disable
+   d shell svc data disable
+   d shell settings get global airplane_mode_on > "$run/offline.airplane"
+   d shell ip -4 route show table all | awk '$1=="default"' > "$run/offline.ipv4"
+   d shell ip -6 route show table all | awk '$1=="default"' > "$run/offline.ipv6"
+   d shell am force-stop --user "$active_user" "$pkg"
+   d shell pidof -s "$pkg"   # Expect no PID.
+   d shell am start --user "$active_user" -n "$activity"
+   # Tap Open signed checklist and wait for the saved sequence 2.
+   d shell pidof -s "$pkg" > "$run/offline.pid"
+   screen_xml > "$run/offline.xml"
+   state "$active_user" > "$run/offline-live.json"
+   workspace "$active_user" > "$run/offline.workspace"
+   # Tap Done and wait for the dialog to close.
+   state "$active_user" > "$run/offline-retired.json"
+   python3 -B "$driver" finish "$packet" "$run"
+   ```
+
+Expect the same healthy candidate at a new launch and in a new process.
+Compare the workspace bytes to the packet seed. `finish` writes
+`android-halt-result.json` and acknowledges the Phoenix fixture. Require
+one passing ExUnit test and **Removed owned PostgreSQL and fixture scratch**.
+
+Remove the exact device XML and shut down the owned emulator. Remove the
+disposable emulator data and private ADB server after closure. Record the
+origin, relay, and emulator teardown, the released ports, and any retained
+path. Keep the compact receipt and the signed packet together.
+
+## Interpret the result
+
+The pending spool holds an interrupted HTTP response. It carries no local
+assignment authority and remains separate from the recovery store's signed
+pending candidate. The halt stops new offers. Historical artifact bytes still
+resolve in the server. A previously downloaded, valid signed offer can
+remain eligible to activate. If the client later receives a compatible signed
+offer, the updater can compare the replayed prefix and continue. An HTTP 204
+provides no offer to resume against.
+
+For the Android user argument order, see the
+[AOSP run-as implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aosp-mirror/platform_system_core/master/run-as/run-as.cpp).
